    "result_text": "The generated mapper confirms the auto-mapping: `ownerDto.setMembershipLevel( owner.getMembershipLevel() )`. \n\nThe finding was valid \u2014 I've consolidated the duplicated rule into a single source.\n\n## What I changed\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived, `@Transient` `getMembershipLevel()` as the one home for the rule (start at 1, +1 for email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, cap at 3; level 4 reserved for tenure). Safe because the entity uses JPA FIELD access (the `@Id` is on a field), so Hibernate ignores the getter for persistence, and the REST layer serializes DTOs rather than the entity.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Dropped the explicit `@Mapping` expression and the `toMembershipLevel` default method; MapStruct now auto-maps `membershipLevel` by name straight from `owner.getMembershipLevel()`.\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 The audit line now calls `owner.getMembershipLevel()` and the duplicated private helper is removed.\n\nThe OpenAPI schema change and the field rename remain as before. One definition of the rule now feeds both the DTO and the audit line.\n\nBuild is green: `BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance test passes, and the audit line still emits `membershipLevel=3`.",
